From: Cristian Papa <76759272+Cris7015@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mtd: spinand: handle BMT attach failures safely

Do not expose writable SPI-NAND when an explicitly requested BMT cannot be
attached.  Keep the device registered for diagnosis, but clear its writable
flag.  Also force read-only exposure when the EcoNet BMT diagnostic mode
was requested successfully.

Signed-off-by: Cristian Papa <76759272+Cris7015@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/drivers/mtd/nand/spi/core.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/nand/spi/core.c
@@ -1751,7 +1751,17 @@ static int spinand_probe(struct spi_mem
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
-	mtk_bmt_attach(mtd);
+	ret = mtk_bmt_attach(mtd);
+	if (ret) {
+		dev_err(&mem->spi->dev,
+			"BMT attach failed (%d), forcing MTD read-only\n", ret);
+		mtd->flags &= ~MTD_WRITEABLE;
+	} else if (of_property_read_bool(mem->spi->dev.of_node,
+					 "econet,bmt-read-only")) {
+		dev_info(&mem->spi->dev,
+			 "BMT diagnostic mode, forcing MTD read-only\n");
+		mtd->flags &= ~MTD_WRITEABLE;
+	}
 	ret = mtd_device_register(mtd, NULL, 0);
 	if (ret)
 		goto err_spinand_cleanup;
